******************************************************** Rgndefs Equates** Rgndefs.Equs contains equates used in the following* calls:**    _OpenRgn    _CloseRgn    _SectRgn    _DiffRgn*    _UnionRgn   _XorRgn      _PtInRgn    _RectInRgn*    _InsetRgn   _OffsetRgn   _MapRgn     _MapRect*    _MapPt** and in the following region assembly routines:**    PutLine     PutRect      PutRgn** Globals variables used by these routines (commonly used variables* and variables used for intercommunication) are found in the first* section.  The variables which follow consist of three* distinct (overlapping) sets of variables.  The first set is used* by the Put and Map routines, the second by the region packing* routines, and the third by the region operation routines.******************************************************** Just so we can make things clearer, let's define what the bounding box* of a region looks like.BBoxLen        equ 0BBoxTop        equ 2BBoxLeft       equ 4BBoxBottom     equ 6BBoxRight      equ 8* These comprise a rectangle we use for various shortcut paths in SECTRGN* and for holding values for PutRect and PutLine.RgnY1          equ Rect2RgnX1          equ RgnY1+2RgnY2          equ RgnX1+2RgnX2          equ RgnY2+2* These are general purpose variables which are frequently used.  BufHandle* and BufPtr are used to manage any active inversion point list.Dv             equ RgnX2+2             ; general purpose parameters forDh             equ Dv+2                ; inset, offset, and other usesOp             equ Dh+2                ; operation used in SectRgn, etcBufHandle      equ Op+2                ; handle for inversion point bufferBufPtr         equ BufHandle+4         ; pointer for inversion point bufferPtCount        equ BufPtr+4            ; point count for Pack, Sort, CullEndOfRgnRect   equ PtCount+2* Zero page usage by PutRgn, PutLine, PutRect, MapRgn, MapRect, and MapPtIndex          equ EndOfRgnRect        ; overlaps iptrSrcY           equ Index+2             ; overlaps jptrDeltaX         equ SrcY+2DeltaY         equ DeltaX+2Slope          equ DeltaY+2Horiz          equ Slope+4V              equ Horiz+4H              equ V+2FRect          equ H+2                ; MapRgn, MapRect, MapPtTRect          equ FRect+8LastPt         equ TRect+8LastY          equ LastPt+2Counter        equ LastY+2MapV           equ Counter+2MapH           equ MapV+2Sign           equ MapH+2DifHeight      equ Sign+2DifWidth       equ DifHeight+2FHeight        equ DifWidth+2FWidth         equ FHeight+2;------------------------------------------------------;; Change in equates from what is in ROM to get these; four back on zero page;THeight        equ MinRect             ; MinRect since it is not usedTWidth         equ THeight+2           ; during mappingHeightRound    equ TWidth+2            ;WidthRound     equ HeightRound+2* PutOval EquatesOLeftEdge      equ Index+2ORightEdge     equ OLeftEdge+4OvalY          equ ORightEdge+4Square         equ OvalY+2Rsqysq         equ Square+8OddNum         equ Rsqysq+4OddBump        equ OddNum+8SkipTop        equ OddBump+8SkipBot        equ SkipTop+2OOldLeft       equ SkipBot+2OOldRight      equ OOldLeft+2* Zero page usage by PackRgn, SortPoints, and CullPointsiptr           equ EndOfRgnRect         ; Pack,Sortjptr           equ iptr+2               ; Pack,SortMinH           equ jptr+2               ; PackMaxH           equ MinH+2               ; PackCurY           equ MaxH+2               ; Packlptr           equ CurY+2               ; Sortrptr           equ lptr+2               ; SortMidV           equ rptr+2               ; SortMidH           equ MidV+2               ; SortSpCount        equ MidH+2               ; SortSluff          equ SpCount+2            ; CullNextY          equ Sluff+2              ; CullDestY          equ NextY+2              ; CullPointV         equ DestY+2              ; CullPointH         equ PointV+2             ; Cull* Zero page usage for _SectRgn, _UnionRgn, _DiffRgn, and _XorRgn, as* well as supporting routines.  The associated files are SECTRGN,* RGNOP, and RGNSCAN.  If we couldn't take any shortcuts, we probably have a* lot more work to do.  These variables describe the general state of things* as we begin and continue the RgnOp procedure.  A new handle is allocated* for an inversion point list and it's placed in BufHandle.  ListPtr and* ListMax refer to this handle (so we don't have to continually index into* Bufptr to get them).  NextA and NextB keep track of the vertical* scan line as we examine the source regions.* PtrBaseA is either RgnPtrA or Scratch, the latter if the region is* rectangular (in which case we create a fake expanded region from the* bounding box).  The same applies to PtrBaseB.  PtrA and PtrB are the* indexes (used in the y register) to the region data.  ScratchHandle* is our work area.  It is divided into five parts, and so five separate* indexes are maintained to point into each part.* The variables starting at SrcBase1 communicate with the scan routines.* They take two sources and a destination, but the second source and* the destination are always somewhere in [Scratch], so the bases are* assumed known.  [SrcBase1] will be equivalent to one of [Scratch],* [PtrBaseA], or [PtrBaseB].  The indexes are set up in Src1, Src2, and Dst.ListPtr        equ EndOfRgnRect         ; current length of BufPtr listListMax        equ ListPtr+2            ; current size of BufPtr listNextA          equ ListMax+2            ; next horizontal point in Src1NextB          equ NextA+2              ; next horizontal point in Src2Vert           equ NextB+2              ; current vertical pointPtrBaseA       equ Vert+2               ; first source regionPtrA           equ PtrBaseA+4           ; index into first source regionPtrBaseB       equ PtrA+2               ; second source regionPtrB           equ PtrBaseB+4           ; index into second source regionScratchHandle  equ PtrB+2               ; handle to our work areaScratch        equ ScratchHandle+4      ; pointer to our 5 part work areaScanA          equ Scratch+4            ; index to 1st partScanB          equ ScanA+2              ; index to 2nd partScanC          equ ScanB+2              ; index to 3rd partTempScan       equ ScanC+2              ; index to 4th partOutScan        equ TempScan+2           ; index to 5th partSrcBase1       equ OutScan+2            ; base pointer to first scan listSrc1           equ SrcBase1+4           ; index within SrcBase1Src2           equ Src1+2               ; index within SrcBase2Dst            equ Src2+2               ; index to dst within Scratch* These state flags are used in RgnScan as it examines and combines the* inversion points from [SrcBase1],Src1 and [SrcBase2],Src2* These variables use space in the region equates not used* until drawing occurs.Next1          equ End2Regions          ; next H coord in Src1Next2          equ Next1+2              ; next H coord in Src2State1         equ Next2+2              ; state toggle for 1st scan sourceState2         equ State1+2             ; state toggle for 2nd scan sourceOldRight       equ State2+2             ; a counterzzzEndOfRdfs   equ Dst+2